<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Microalgae Biofuel Growth Rate</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f7f6;
            color: #333;
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .container {
            background: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        .math-box {
            background: #eef2f5;
            padding: 15px;
            border-left: 4px solid #2c3e50;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            font-family: monospace;
            font-size: 1.1em;
        }
        #info-panel {
            margin-top: 20px;
            padding: 15px;
            background: #e8f5e9;
            border: 1px solid #c8e6c9;
            border-radius: 5px;
            display: none;
        }
        .source-text {
            font-size: 0.85em;
            color: #666;
            margin-top: 10px;
            font-style: italic;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
    <h2>Optimizing Algae Biomass for Biofuel Production</h2>
    <p>To maximize bio-jet fuel yield, we need to harvest microalgae when its growth rate is at its absolute peak. The graph below shows the total biomass concentration over 30 days.</p>
    
    <div class="math-box">
        <strong>Biomass Function (Total Yield):</strong><br>
        f(t) = 2.5 / (1 + 9e<sup>-0.3t</sup>) g/L<br><br>
        <strong>Derivative Function (Daily Growth Rate):</strong><br>
        f'(t) = (6.75e<sup>-0.3t</sup>) / (1 + 9e<sup>-0.3t</sup>)<sup>2</sup> g/L per day
    </div>

    <p><em>Click on any data point on the curve to calculate the derivative (growth rate) at that exact moment.</em></p>

    <canvas id="growthChart" width="400" height="200"></canvas>
    
    <div id="info-panel">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #2e7d32;">Analysis at Day <span id="day-display"></span></h3>
        <p><strong>Total Biomass f(t):</strong> <span id="biomass-display"></span> g/L</p>
        <p><strong>Rate of Change f'(t):</strong> <span id="derivative-display"></span> g/L per day</p>
        <p><strong>What this means:</strong> <span id="layman-explanation"></span></p>
    </div>

    <p class="source-text">Data source: Simulated model based on Malaysian Palm Oil Board (MPOB) and local university bioenergy research on Chlorella vulgaris cultivation in POME.</p>
</div>

<script>
    // Mathematical setup
    const calculateBiomass = (t) => 2.5 / (1 + 9 * Math.exp(-0.3 * t));
    const calculateDerivative = (t) => {
        const expTerm = Math.exp(-0.3 * t);
        return (6.75 * expTerm) / Math.pow((1 + 9 * expTerm), 2);
    };

    // Generate data points for 30 days
    const days = Array.from({length: 31}, (_, i) => i);
    const biomassData = days.map(t => calculateBiomass(t));

    // Chart.js initialization
    const ctx = document.getElementById('growthChart').getContext('2d');
    const growthChart = new Chart(ctx, {
        type: 'line',
        data: {
            labels: days,
            datasets: [{
                label: 'Biomass Concentration (g/L)',
                data: biomassData,
                borderColor: '#2ecc71',
                backgroundColor: 'rgba(46, 204, 113, 0.2)',
                borderWidth: 3,
                pointBackgroundColor: '#27ae60',
                pointRadius: 4,
                pointHoverRadius: 7,
                fill: true,
                tension: 0.4
            }]
        },
        options: {
            responsive: true,
            animation: {
                duration: 2000,
                easing: 'easeOutQuart'
            },
            scales: {
                x: {
                    title: { display: true, text: 'Time (Days)' }
                },
                y: {
                    title: { display: true, text: 'Biomass (g/L)' },
                    min: 0,
                    max: 3
                }
            },
            onClick: (e, activeElements) => {
                if (activeElements.length > 0) {
                    const dataIndex = activeElements[0].index;
                    const day = days[dataIndex];
                    const biomass = biomassData[dataIndex];
                    const rate = calculateDerivative(day);
                    
                    updatePanel(day, biomass, rate);
                }
            }
        }
    });

    // Update the UI panel with derivative explanation
    function updatePanel(day, biomass, rate) {
        document.getElementById('info-panel').style.display = 'block';
        document.getElementById('day-display').innerText = day;
        document.getElementById('biomass-display').innerText = biomass.toFixed(3);
        document.getElementById('derivative-display').innerText = rate.toFixed(4);

        let explanation = "";
        if (day < 7) {
            explanation = "The algae are just getting used to the environment. The derivative (growth rate) is low because the population is small, so they aren't multiplying very fast yet.";
        } else if (day >= 7 && day <= 12) {
            explanation = "This is the exponential phase. The derivative is hitting its maximum value. The algae are reproducing rapidly, making this the most productive time for the bioreactor.";
        } else if (day > 12 && day < 20) {
            explanation = "Growth is slowing down. The derivative is decreasing because the algae are running out of nutrients in the effluent and crowding each other out.";
        } else {
            explanation = "The population has stabilized. The derivative is close to zero, meaning new algae growth perfectly balances out cell death. This is the absolute latest you should harvest.";
        }
        
        document.getElementById('layman-explanation').innerText = explanation;
    }
</script>

</body>
</html>
